IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P2-art-20.l4 -- ARTICLE 20 OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679: RIGHT TO DATA PORTABILITY (layer 1).
-- Written by P2 (Sonnet 5.5).  Lines 253-260 of eu-gdpr-2016-679-consolidated-20160504.txt (the two heading lines of
-- Article 20 at 253-254 are `inert` headings; the Section 4 heading at 261-262 belongs to Article 21).
-- Target compiler: main (build 1.6.112).  Answers: MAYBE BOOLEAN for the rights, a DEONTIC for the regulative rule.
-- WHOSE.  The data subject's CLAIM against the controller (to receive the data; to transmit them to another controller
-- "without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided"); the controller's duty is its
-- correlative, and its prohibition (SHANT) is the one regulative rule.  ARTICLE 11(2): see P2-art-15.l4.
-- THE CONDITIONS of paragraph 1 ("where: (a) ... and (b) ...") are read in `Art 20(1) ... receive ...`; the transmit
-- right has the same conditions and calls it.
-- READING A RESULT (NOTES).  NOTHING means the Regulation does not answer on these facts; never read it as no.
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 20 action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 20(1) hinder the transmission of the personal data to another controller`
    `Art 20(1) provide the data subject with the personal data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format`
    `Art 20(2) transmit the personal data directly to another controller`

§ `Article 20(3): the limits of the right`

-- src:259 | 3. The exercise of the right referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall be without prejudice to Article 17. That right shall not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller.
@ref Art 20(3), both sentences (src:259)
GIVEN `the data subject exercises the right referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(3) the exercise of the right referred to in paragraph 1 prejudices the right to erasure under Article 17` MEANS
    IF `the data subject exercises the right referred to in paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "The exercise of the right referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall be without prejudice to Article 17"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The exercise of the right referred to in paragraph 1": a case with no exercise of the right is outside the sentence

-- src:259 | That right shall not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller.
@ref Art 20(3) second sentence (src:259)
GIVEN `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(3) the right to data portability does not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority` MEANS
    IF `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means the right does not apply): "That right shall not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "That right shall not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task ...": other processing is outside the sentence, and whether the right applies to it is decided by paragraph 1

-- src:260 | 4. The right referred to in paragraph 1 shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others.
@ref Art 20(4) (src:260)
GIVEN `the exercise of the right would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(4) the right referred to in paragraph 1 is limited because its exercise would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others` MEANS
    IF `the exercise of the right would adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative; JUST TRUE here means the limit applies): "shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others"; JUST TRUE here means the limit applies
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not adversely affect the rights and freedoms of others": where the exercise has no such effect the limit is not engaged and the paragraph is silent

§ `Article 20(1): the right to receive and the right to transmit`

-- src:255 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her, which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format and have the right to transmit those data to another controller without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided, where:
-- src:256 | (a) the processing is based on consent pursuant to point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2) or on a contract pursuant to point (b) of Article 6(1); and
-- src:257 | (b) the processing is carried out by automated means.
@ref Art 20(1) chapeau and points (a) and (b): the right to receive (src:255-257)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data concerning the data subject were provided by the data subject to the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the processing is carried out by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The data subject shall have the right to receive ... to a controller": a grant to the data subject (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF `Art 20(3) the right to data portability does not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "shall not apply"): "That right shall not apply to processing necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller"
        IF NOT (`the personal data concerning the data subject were provided by the data subject to the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the personal data concerning him or her, which he or she has provided to a controller": data the data subject did not provide are outside the grant (fork F20-1)
        IF NOT (`the processing is carried out by automated means`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); a right named as an entitlement, fork F15-1): "where: ... (b) the processing is carried out by automated means"
        IF `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` OR `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the processing is based on a contract pursuant to point (b) of Article 6(1) is P1's answer, and it does not answer on these facts
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b)): "where: (a) the processing is based on consent pursuant to point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2) or on a contract pursuant to point (b) of Article 6(1)"
    -- "in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format": the form in which the right is to be met; it gives no input, since the right exists whatever form the controller uses.

GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data concerning the data subject were provided by the data subject to the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the processing is carried out by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to transmit those data to another controller without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided` MEANS
    `Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format` `the person is the data subject` `the body is the controller` `the personal data concerning the data subject were provided by the data subject to the controller` `the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2)` `Art 6(1)(b) point (b) applies` `the processing is carried out by automated means` `the processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in the controller` `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied`
    -- the second right of paragraph 1 has the same conditions as the first ("the right to receive ... and have the right to transmit ... where: (a) ... and (b) ..."): one answer for both (fork F20-2)

GIVEN `Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to transmit those data to another controller without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 20 action`
`Art 20(1) the controller shall not hinder the transmission of the personal data to another controller` MEANS
    IF `Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to transmit those data to another controller without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         SHANT `Art 20(1) hinder the transmission of the personal data to another controller`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- a SHANT with no deadline is breached by the act itself

-- src:255 | 1. The data subject shall have the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her, which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format and have the right to transmit those data to another controller without hindrance from the controller to which the personal data have been provided, where:
-- src:256 | (a) the processing is based on consent pursuant to point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2) or on a contract pursuant to point (b) of Article 6(1); and
-- src:257 | (b) the processing is carried out by automated means.
@ref Art 20(1) the controller's duty to provide the data (the right to receive) (src:255-257)
GIVEN `Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 20 action`
`Art 20(1) the controller must give the data subject the personal data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format` MEANS
    IF `Art 20(1) the data subject has the right to receive the personal data concerning him or her which he or she has provided to a controller, in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 20(1) provide the data subject with the personal data in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the text names the controller to which the data were provided ("which he or she has provided to a controller") and the act (providing them in that format); no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path); the rule takes the answer of the right (R8)

§ `Article 20(2): direct transmission from one controller to another`

-- src:258 | 2. In exercising his or her right to data portability pursuant to paragraph 1, the data subject shall have the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another, where technically feasible.
@ref Art 20(2) (src:258)
GIVEN `the person is the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject exercises the right to data portability pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `direct transmission from one controller to another is technically feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 20(2) the data subject has the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another, where technically feasible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the data subject` AND `the body is the controller`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the data subject shall have the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another": a grant to the data subject (entitlement-named, fork F15-1)
        IF `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, Article 11(2)): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject"
        IF NOT (`the data subject exercises the right to data portability pursuant to paragraph 1`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In exercising his or her right to data portability pursuant to paragraph 1": a case outside the exercise of that right is outside the sentence, which has no gate word (ruling (c))
        IF NOT (`direct transmission from one controller to another is technically feasible`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where", periods ruling (b); a right named as an entitlement, fork F15-1): "where technically feasible"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:258 | 2. In exercising his or her right to data portability pursuant to paragraph 1, the data subject shall have the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another, where technically feasible.
@ref Art 20(2) the controller's duty to transmit directly (src:258)
GIVEN `Art 20(2) the data subject has the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another, where technically feasible` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 20 action`
`Art 20(2) the controller must transmit the personal data directly to another controller` MEANS
    IF `Art 20(2) the data subject has the right to have the personal data transmitted directly from one controller to another, where technically feasible` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY controller
         MUST `Art 20(2) transmit the personal data directly to another controller`
    ELSE FULFILLED
    -- the text names the transmitting controller ("from one controller to another") and the act (transmitting directly), "where technically feasible" being a gate of the right that the right's answer already carries; no time limit and no consequence is stated (NOTES, Rules with no breach path) (R8)
